#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# euler_gamma

#% text
# `euler_gamma` is Euler's constant `gamma = 0.5772...`, the limit of `1 + 1/2 + ... + 1/n - log(n)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `euler_gamma` is exact and known to be a positive real; `n(euler_gamma, d)` gives `d` digits, computed by the Brent-McMillan method.

#% item
# It appears in special values such as `digamma(1) = -euler_gamma`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
euler_gamma
#% output
#= euler_gamma

#% cell
n(euler_gamma, 40)
#% output
#= 0.57721566490153286060651209008240243104215934

#% cell
digamma(1)
#% output
#= -euler_gamma

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The slow limit of the harmonic numbers minus the logarithm; the difference is about `1/(2n)`:

#% cell
n(harmonic_number(1000) - log(1000)) - n(euler_gamma)
#% output
#= 0.0004999166666753707

#% text
# The derivative of `gamma` at 1:

#% cell
d(gamma(x), x) /. x -> 1
#% output
#= -euler_gamma

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `digamma`, `harmonic_number`, `e`, `pi`
